msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versioni dei pacchetti\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il codice in questa pagina è stato sviluppato utilizzando i seguenti requisiti.\n"
"Ti consigliamo di utilizzare queste versioni o successive.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A quantum-classical workflow runs as one managed workflow job. Its classical stages run on your compute profile, and the primitive jobs that it sends to an IBM Quantum&reg; QPU run on your instance and count against your usage. From that one job, you can report each stage, find the QPU jobs, and cancel them. To start a job and check its status and logs, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Un workflow quantistico-classico viene eseguito come un unico job di workflow gestito. Le sue fasi classiche vengono eseguite sul tuo profilo di calcolo, mentre i job primitive che invia a una QPU di IBM Quantum&reg; vengono eseguiti sulla tua istanza e contano ai fini del tuo utilizzo. Da quel singolo job puoi segnalare ogni fase, trovare i job QPU e annullarli. Per avviare un job e controllarne stato e log, consulta [Esegui un workflow gestito](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Prima di iniziare, [distribuisci il tuo primo workflow gestito](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service {#create-the-runtime-service}"
msgstr "Crea il servizio Runtime {#create-the-runtime-service}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service in your workflow code with `get_runtime_service()`, and use it in the same way that you use `QiskitRuntimeService` locally. The following workflow runs a Bell circuit with the Sampler primitive, reports each stage with `update_status()`, and returns the counts:\n"
msgstr "Crea il servizio Runtime nel codice del tuo workflow con `get_runtime_service()` e usalo allo stesso modo in cui usi `QiskitRuntimeService` in locale. Il workflow seguente esegue un circuito di Bell con la primitive Sampler, segnala ogni fase con `update_status()` e restituisce i conteggi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_runtime_service()` returns a `QiskitRuntimeService` that is set up for your managed workflow job, and it provides the following:\n"
msgstr "`get_runtime_service()` restituisce un `QiskitRuntimeService` configurato per il tuo job di workflow gestito e fornisce quanto segue:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Credentials.** The Runtime service uses the API key, instance, and channel that you used to call `run()`, so the workflow code needs no credentials.\n"
msgstr "**Credenziali.** Il servizio Runtime usa la chiave API, l'istanza e il canale che hai usato per chiamare `run()`, quindi il codice del workflow non richiede credenziali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Tracking.** A workflow records every primitive job that runs through this Runtime service under the managed workflow job, including Sampler, Estimator, and Executor jobs, and jobs in a session or batch. You can list them with `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "**Tracciamento.** Un workflow registra ogni job primitive eseguito tramite questo servizio Runtime sotto il job di workflow gestito, inclusi i job Sampler, Estimator ed Executor e i job in una sessione o in un batch. Puoi elencarli con `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cancellation.** When you call `job.cancel()`, the managed workflow also cancels the workflow's sessions, batches, and primitive jobs that are still running.\n"
msgstr "**Annullamento.** Quando chiami `job.cancel()`, il workflow gestito annulla anche le sessioni, i batch e i job primitive del workflow ancora in esecuzione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not track or cancel the jobs of a service that you create with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, although the jobs still run. If the workflow must use another service, cancel its jobs in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Un workflow gestito non traccia né annulla i job di un servizio creato con `QiskitRuntimeService()`, anche se i job vengono comunque eseguiti. Se il workflow deve usare un altro servizio, annulla i suoi job in un [gestore `SIGTERM`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run primitives in a session or batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"
msgstr "Esegui le primitive in una sessione o in un batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow also tracks primitive jobs that run in a session or batch. Create the session or batch from a backend that the Runtime service returned, and create the primitives inside the `with` block. `Session` works in the same way:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow gestito traccia anche i job primitive eseguiti in una sessione o in un batch. Crea la sessione o il batch da un backend restituito dal servizio Runtime e crea le primitive all'interno del blocco `with`. `Session` funziona allo stesso modo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report progress with update_status() {#report-progress-with-update-status}"
msgstr "Segnala l'avanzamento con update_status() {#report-progress-with-update-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow in [Create the Runtime service](#create-the-runtime-service) calls `update_status()` at the start of each stage, so that the job status shows where the workflow is, such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Pass one of the following `Job` constants:\n"
msgstr "Il workflow in [Crea il servizio Runtime](#create-the-runtime-service) chiama `update_status()` all'inizio di ogni fase, in modo che lo stato del job mostri a che punto si trova il workflow, ad esempio `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Passa una delle seguenti costanti `Job`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call in the workflow | Job status |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Chiamata nel workflow | Stato del job |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status()` returns `True` if the workflow changed the status. It returns `False` and writes a warning to the logs if the value is not one of these constants, if the job is no longer active, or if the code runs outside a job. It does not raise an error, so a typo does not stop the workflow.\n"
msgstr "`update_status()` restituisce `True` se il workflow ha cambiato lo stato. Restituisce `False` e scrive un avviso nei log se il valore non è una di queste costanti, se il job non è più attivo o se il codice viene eseguito fuori da un job. Non solleva un errore, quindi un refuso non interrompe il workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For progress within a stage, such as the iterations of an optimizer, [write log lines](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"
msgstr "Per l'avanzamento all'interno di una fase, come le iterazioni di un ottimizzatore, [scrivi righe di log](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: each update_status() call writes a SUB_STATUS_CHANGE event, and the 24-hour timeout is measured from the job's latest event (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py _timed_out). send_error() events count too. This looks like a bug; do not document it until the intended behavior is confirmed. */}\n"
msgstr ""

