# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow, and pass the name of the backend when you run it:\n"
msgstr "Carica il workflow e passa il nome del backend quando lo esegui:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job ends, get the IDs of the workflow's QPU jobs from the managed workflow job:\n"
msgstr "Dopo la conclusione del job, ottieni dal job di workflow gestito gli ID dei job QPU del workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each ID is a regular primitive job ID. To read a job's status and results, see [Retrieve job results at a later time](/guides/monitor-job#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time).\n"
"If the workflow ran primitives in a session or batch, list the session and batch IDs with `runtime_sessions()`, and pass one to `runtime_jobs()` to get only the jobs in it:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ogni ID è un normale ID di job primitive. Per leggere lo stato e i risultati di un job, consulta [Recupera i risultati di un job in un secondo momento](/guides/monitor-job#retrieve-job-results-at-a-later-time).\n"
"Se il workflow ha eseguito primitive in una sessione o in un batch, elenca gli ID di sessione e batch con `runtime_sessions()` e passane uno a `runtime_jobs()` per ottenere solo i job al suo interno:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `job` object exists only in the notebook that started the run. In a new notebook, get the job again with `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, then call `runtime_jobs()` on it. See [Find a job from a new session](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"
msgstr "L'oggetto `job` esiste solo nel notebook che ha avviato l'esecuzione. In un nuovo notebook, ottieni di nuovo il job con `client.job(\"<your-job-id>\")`, quindi chiama `runtime_jobs()` su di esso. Consulta [Trova un job da una nuova sessione](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-a-job-from-a-new-session).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the QPU usage and run times of each QPU job, see [View job metrics](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). For the usage of your whole instance in the current period, call `client.usage()`. To see how long each stage of the managed workflow job took, see [Check how long each stage took](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"
msgstr "Per l'utilizzo della QPU e i tempi di esecuzione di ogni job QPU, consulta [Visualizza le metriche del job](/guides/monitor-job#view-job-metrics). Per l'utilizzo dell'intera istanza nel periodo corrente, chiama `client.usage()`. Per vedere quanto è durata ogni fase del job di workflow gestito, consulta [Controlla quanto è durata ogni fase](/guides/run-managed-workflow#check-how-long-each-stage-took).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel linked QPU jobs {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"
msgstr "Annulla i job QPU collegati {#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a managed workflow job with `job.cancel()`, the workflow also tries to cancel the QPU work that the workflow started:\n"
msgstr "Quando annulli un job di workflow gestito con `job.cancel()`, il workflow prova anche ad annullare il lavoro QPU che ha avviato:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions and batches.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's sessions and batches, which also cancels their queued jobs.\n"
msgstr "**Sessioni e batch.** Il workflow annulla ogni sessione e ogni batch del workflow, il che annulla anche i loro job in coda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other primitive jobs.** The workflow cancels each of the workflow's other primitive jobs that are still queued or running.\n"
msgstr "**Altri job primitive.** Il workflow annulla ogni altro job primitive del workflow ancora in coda o in esecuzione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message for each QPU job and session, so you can check what was canceled:\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` restituisce un messaggio per ogni job QPU e sessione, così puoi verificare cosa è stato annullato:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a workflow that ran in a batch, the message looks like the following:\n"
msgstr "Per un workflow eseguito in un batch, il messaggio è simile al seguente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the client cannot create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, it cancels only the managed workflow job. Cancel the QPU jobs yourself with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Se il client non riesce a creare un `QiskitRuntimeService` dalle tue credenziali locali, annulla solo il job di workflow gestito. Annulla tu stesso i job QPU con i loro ID da `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a workflow stops a job itself, for example because it reached the 24-hour limit, it does not cancel its QPU jobs. Cancel them with their IDs from `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "Quando un workflow interrompe un job da sé, ad esempio perché ha raggiunto il limite di 24 ore, non annulla i suoi job QPU. Annullali con i loro ID da `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the scheduler's timeout and blocked-account stops (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout, FleetsJobCanceller) cancel only the fleet. Only the user stop endpoint (StopJobUseCase) cancels runtime jobs. Confirm whether this is intended before publishing. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot QPU jobs in a workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Risoluzione dei problemi dei job QPU in un workflow {#troubleshoot-qpu-jobs-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` raises `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | The code runs in your local notebook, not in a managed workflow job. Use `QiskitRuntimeService()` locally. |\n"
"| `update_status()` returns `False`, and the logs show `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | The value is not one of the `Job` constants, or the job is no longer active. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` returns `[]`. | The workflow created its service with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, or it has not run a primitive yet. |\n"
"| A session's jobs are not tracked. | The session was created from a backend of a different service. Get the backend from `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| The workflow logs show `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | The workflow could not record a primitive job. The primitive job still runs, but it is not tracked. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` shows `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | The client could not create a `QiskitRuntimeService` from your local credentials, so it canceled only the managed workflow job. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fails with `Job [...] not found`. | The job ID is wrong, or the job belongs to another user. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `get_runtime_service()` solleva `KeyError: 'QISKIT_IBM_CHANNEL'`. | Il codice viene eseguito nel tuo notebook locale, non in un job di workflow gestito. Usa `QiskitRuntimeService()` in locale. |\n"
"| `update_status()` restituisce `False` e i log mostrano `'sub_status' not provided or is not valid`. | Il valore non è una delle costanti `Job`, oppure il job non è più attivo. |\n"
"| `job.runtime_jobs()` restituisce `[]`. | Il workflow ha creato il suo servizio con `QiskitRuntimeService()`, oppure non ha ancora eseguito una primitive. |\n"
"| I job di una sessione non vengono tracciati. | La sessione è stata creata da un backend di un servizio diverso. Ottieni il backend da `get_runtime_service()`. |\n"
"| I log del workflow mostrano `Could not associate runtime job with serverless job`. | Il workflow non è riuscito a registrare un job primitive. Il job primitive viene comunque eseguito, ma non viene tracciato. |\n"
"| `job.cancel()` mostra `No QiskitRuntimeService can be associated to the given token and instance.` | Il client non è riuscito a creare un `QiskitRuntimeService` dalle tue credenziali locali, quindi ha annullato solo il job di workflow gestito. |\n"
"| `client.job()` fallisce con `Job [...] not found`. | L'ID del job è errato, oppure il job appartiene a un altro utente. |\n"

